-A method to model infinite regular 3D lattices by defining parallel slabs using periodic trigonometric functions, intersecting them to form rods, and uniting the rods [S1]. It is chosen when a periodic, infinite cellular structure is required. It differs from finite lattice representations by being defined analytically over the entire domain. [S1]
