 ### Microstructure-External Shape Combination
-A method to combine an infinite microstructure lattice with a given external object shape by creating a thin shell and intersecting the lattice with the object [S1]. It is chosen when embedding internal structures within a specific boundary. It differs from simple clipping by using R-function subtraction to maintain smooth shell thickness. [S1]
