 ## Operating characteristics
 
-*   **Time Complexity**: Evaluation is $O(1)$ per point query, involving a constant number of trigonometric, square root, and arithmetic operations. The cost depends on the depth of the boolean tree (number of nested operations).
-*   **Memory Complexity**: $O(1)$ for procedural evaluation, as no grid or mesh data is stored. Parameters are stored in constant space.
-*   **Measured Performance**: Not given in the sources.
-*   **Scaling**: The method scales well with resolution since it is procedural. However, evaluating deep boolean trees or complex lattices with many parameters increases computational cost per sample.
