 ## Background
 
-The method originates from the Function Representation (FRep) approach to procedural modeling, which addresses the drawbacks of Boundary Representation (BRep) and voxel-based models [S1]. R-functions were introduced by Rabinovich and later developed by Shapiro and others for implicit modeling [S1]. The specific application to microstructures and lattices using trigonometric functions was proposed in the paper "Procedural function-based modelling of volumetric microstructures" [S1]. This work builds on earlier applications of implicit surfaces to biological cells and periodic structures like chess boards [S1].
